Build **Carom**, a top-down paddle duel that runs entirely in the browser.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Build the game there. Its dependencies
are already installed, so you can build and test right away.

## What to read first

The full specification is in `{{workspace}}/specs/`, already present in your
project. Produce an implementation that matches it exactly. Start with
`specs/overview.md`: it states what you implement, which files stay as they are,
the code quality the build is held to, and the commands that run over the
finished repository.

## The build interface

`npm ci` then `npm run build` produces the static site into `dist/` at the
project root, with no other manual step.

## Driving the game in a browser

Playwright and a headless Chromium are installed in this project. There is no
global Playwright on `PATH`; it lives in `node_modules` like any other
dependency, so it is imported from the project (for example
`import { chromium } from "playwright"`) or run with `npx playwright`. This
container has no Chromium sandbox, so Chromium launches with the `--no-sandbox`
argument.

## Commit your work

Your project root is a git repository, initialized before you started with the
starter files in its first commit. Your finished implementation is published
from this repository's commits, so leave a clean working tree: everything
committed, nothing untracked. A `.gitignore` already excludes `node_modules/`,
the build output, and coverage reports.
